  ('BOAST', 'Jeremiah 9:23', 'This is what the LORD says: Let not the wise boast of their wisdom or the strong boast of their strength or the rich boast of their riches.', NOW()),
  ('BOOKS', 'Revelation 20:12', 'And I saw the dead, great and small, standing before the throne, and books were opened.', NOW()),
  ('BOWLS', 'Revelation 15:7', 'Then one of the four living creatures gave to the seven angels seven golden bowls filled with the wrath of God.', NOW()),
  ('BURNT', 'Psalm 51:16', 'You do not delight in sacrifice, or I would bring it; you do not take pleasure in burnt offerings.', NOW()),
  ('BURST', 'Job 32:19', 'Inside I am like bottled-up wine, like new wineskins ready to burst.', NOW()),
  ('CARES', '1 Peter 5:7', 'Cast all your anxiety on him because he cares for you.', NOW()),
  ('CHAIN', 'Acts 28:20', 'For this reason I have asked to see you and talk with you. It is because of the hope of Israel that I am bound with this chain.', NOW()),
  ('CHEEK', 'Matthew 5:39', 'But I tell you, do not resist an evil person. If anyone slaps you on the right cheek, turn to them the other cheek also.', NOW()),
  ('CHOKE', 'Mark 4:19', 'But the worries of this life, the deceitfulness of wealth and the desires for other things come in and choke the word, making it unfruitful.', NOW()),
  ('CLAIM', 'John 10:33', 'We are not stoning you for any good work, they replied, but for blasphemy, because you, a mere man, claim to be God.', NOW()),
  ('COAST', 'Acts 27:2', 'We boarded a ship from Adramyttium about to sail for ports along the coast of the province of Asia.', NOW()),
  ('COINS', 'Luke 15:8', 'Or suppose a woman has ten silver coins and loses one. Does she not light a lamp, sweep the house and search carefully until she finds it?', NOW()),
  ('CORDS', 'John 2:15', 'So he made a whip out of cords, and drove all from the temple courts, both sheep and cattle.', NOW()),
  ('DEPTH', 'Romans 8:39', 'Neither height nor depth, nor anything else in all creation, will be able to separate us from the love of God that is in Christ Jesus our Lord.', NOW()),
  ('DIRGE', 'Luke 7:32', 'They are like children sitting in the marketplace and calling out to each other: We played the pipe for you, and you did not dance; we sang a dirge, and you did not cry.', NOW()),
  ('DOORS', 'John 20:19', 'On the evening of that first day of the week, when the disciples were together, with the doors locked for fear of Jewish leaders, Jesus came and stood among them.', NOW()),
  ('EAGER', 'Romans 1:15', 'That is why I am so eager to preach the gospel also to you who are in Rome.', NOW()),
  ('EARLY', 'Mark 16:2', 'Very early on the first day of the week, just after sunrise, they were on their way to the tomb.', NOW()),
  ('ERROR', 'James 5:20', 'Remember this: Whoever turns a sinner from the error of their way will save them from death.', NOW()),
  ('EXALT', 'Psalm 34:3', 'Glorify the LORD with me; let us exalt his name together.', NOW()),
  ('FORDS', 'Joshua 2:7', 'So the men set out in pursuit of the spies on the road that leads to the fords of the Jordan.', NOW()),
  ('FOXES', 'Song of Solomon 2:15', 'Catch for us the foxes, the little foxes that ruin the vineyards, our vineyards that are in bloom.', NOW()),
  ('FROST', 'Job 38:29', 'From whose womb comes the ice? Who gives birth to the frost from the heavens?', NOW()),
  ('GREET', 'Romans 16:16', 'Greet one another with a holy kiss. All the churches of Christ send greetings.', NOW()),
  ('GROPE', 'Job 5:14', 'Darkness comes upon them in the daytime; at noon they grope as in the night.', NOW()),
  ('HASTE', 'Exodus 12:11', 'This is how you are to eat it: with your cloak tucked into your belt, your sandals on your feet and your staff in your hand. Eat it in haste; it is the LORD''s Passover.', NOW()),
  ('HEARD', 'Genesis 3:8', 'Then the man and his wife heard the sound of the LORD God as he was walking in the garden in the cool of the day.', NOW()),
  ('HIRED', 'Luke 15:17', 'When he came to his senses, he said, How many of my father''s hired servants have food to spare, and here I am starving to death!', NOW()),
  ('HORNS', 'Revelation 5:6', 'Then I saw a Lamb, looking as if it had been slain, standing at the center of the throne. He had seven horns and seven eyes.', NOW()),
  ('IVORY', 'Amos 6:4', 'You lie on beds adorned with ivory and lounge on your couches. You dine on choice lambs and fattened calves.', NOW()),
  ('KNOCK', 'Matthew 7:7', 'Ask and it will be given to you; seek and you will find; knock and the door will be opened to you.', NOW()),
  ('LAUGH', 'Genesis 21:6', 'Sarah said, God has brought me laughter, and everyone who hears about this will laugh with me.', NOW()),
  ('LINEN', 'Revelation 19:8', 'Fine linen, bright and clean, was given her to wear. Fine linen stands for the righteous acts of God''s holy people.', NOW()),
  ('LOOSE', 'Isaiah 58:6', 'Is not this the kind of fasting I have chosen: to loose the chains of injustice and untie the cords of the yoke, to set the oppressed free?', NOW()),
  ('MAKER', 'Job 35:10', 'But no one says, Where is God my Maker, who gives songs in the night?', NOW()),
  ('RAINS', 'Joel 2:23', 'Be glad, people of Zion, rejoice in the LORD your God, for he has given you the autumn rains because he is faithful.', NOW()),
  ('REEDS', 'Exodus 2:3', 'But when she could hide him no longer, she got a papyrus basket for him and coated it with tar and pitch. Then she placed the child in it and put it among the reeds along the bank of the Nile.', NOW()),
  ('SEVEN', 'Revelation 1:20', 'The mystery of the seven stars that you saw in my right hand and of the seven golden lampstands is this: The seven stars are the angels of the seven churches.', NOW()),
  ('SHOOT', 'Isaiah 11:1', 'A shoot will come up from the stump of Jesse; from his roots a Branch will bear fruit.', NOW()),
  ('SHORE', 'John 21:4', 'Early in the morning, Jesus stood on the shore, but the disciples did not realize that it was Jesus.', NOW()),
  ('SIEVE', 'Amos 9:9', 'For I will give the command, and I will shake the people of Israel among all the nations as grain is shaken in a sieve.', NOW()),
  ('SLAIN', 'Revelation 5:12', 'Worthy is the Lamb, who was slain, to receive power and wealth and wisdom and strength and honor and glory and praise!', NOW()),
  ('SMOKE', 'Exodus 19:18', 'Mount Sinai was covered with smoke, because the LORD descended on it in fire. The smoke billowed up from it like smoke from a furnace.', NOW()),
  ('SPIES', 'Joshua 2:1', 'Then Joshua son of Nun secretly sent two spies from Shittim. Go, look over the land, he said, especially Jericho.', NOW()),
  ('STUMP', 'Isaiah 6:13', 'But as the terebinth and oak leave stumps when they are cut down, so the holy seed will be the stump in the land.', NOW()),
  ('SWORE', 'Hebrews 6:13', 'When God made his promise to Abraham, since there was no one greater for him to swear by, he swore by himself.', NOW()),
  ('TENTH', 'Genesis 14:20', 'And praise be to God Most High, who delivered your enemies into your hand. Then Abram gave him a tenth of everything.', NOW()),
  ('THIEF', 'John 10:10', 'The thief comes only to steal and kill and destroy; I have come that they may have life, and have it to the full.', NOW()),
  ('TOMBS', 'Matthew 27:53', 'They came out of the tombs after Jesus'' resurrection and went into the holy city and appeared to many people.', NOW()),
  ('TRULY', 'John 3:3', 'Jesus replied, Very truly I tell you, no one can see the kingdom of God unless they are born again.', NOW()),
  ('WAITS', 'Psalm 130:5', 'I wait for the LORD, my whole being waits, and in his word I put my hope.', NOW()),
  ('WOVEN', 'Psalm 139:15', 'My frame was not hidden from you when I was made in the secret place, when I was woven together in the depths of the earth.', NOW()),
  ('CAVES', 'Hebrews 11:38', 'The world was not worthy of them. They wandered in deserts and mountains, living in caves and in holes in the ground.', NOW()),
  ('CURSE', 'Galatians 3:13', 'Christ redeemed us from the curse of the law by becoming a curse for us.', NOW()),
  ('DECAY', 'Acts 2:31', 'Seeing what was to come, he spoke of the resurrection of the Messiah, that he was not abandoned to the realm of the dead, nor did his body see decay.', NOW()),
  ('DIMLY', '1 Corinthians 13:12', 'For now we see only a reflection as in a mirror; we see dimly. But then we shall see face to face.', NOW()),
  ('EQUIP', 'Hebrews 13:21', 'Equip you with everything good for doing his will, and may he work in us what is pleasing to him.', NOW()),
  ('FAVOR', 'Luke 2:52', 'And Jesus grew in wisdom and stature, and in favor with God and man.', NOW()),
  ('GREED', 'Colossians 3:5', 'Put to death, therefore, whatever belongs to your earthly nature: sexual immorality, impurity, lust, evil desires and greed, which is idolatry.', NOW()),
  ('HEDGE', 'Job 1:10', 'Have you not put a hedge around him and his household and everything he has?', NOW()),
  ('JEERS', 'Hebrews 11:36', 'Some faced jeers and flogging, and even chains and imprisonment.', NOW()),
  ('MEANT', 'John 11:13', 'Jesus had been speaking of his death, but his disciples thought he meant natural sleep.', NOW()),
  ('OFTEN', 'Luke 13:34', 'Jerusalem, Jerusalem, you who kill the prophets and stone those sent to you, how often I have longed to gather your children together.', NOW()),
  ('PLACE', 'Revelation 21:3', 'And I heard a loud voice from the throne saying, Look! God''s dwelling place is now among the people.', NOW()),
  ('PLANK', 'Matthew 7:5', 'You hypocrite, first take the plank out of your own eye, and then you will see clearly to remove the speck from your brother''s eye.', NOW()),
  ('SEERS', 'Isaiah 30:10', 'They say to the seers, See no more visions! and to the prophets, Give us no more visions of what is right!', NOW()),
  ('TENTS', 'Psalm 84:10', 'Better is one day in your courts than a thousand elsewhere; I would rather be a doorkeeper in the house of my God than dwell in the tents of the wicked.', NOW()),
  ('THEME', 'Psalm 45:1', 'My heart is stirred by a noble theme as I recite my verses for the king; my tongue is the pen of a skillful writer.', NOW()),
  ('WEEDS', 'Matthew 13:25', 'But while everyone was sleeping, his enemy came and sowed weeds among the wheat, and went away.', NOW()),
  ('YEAST', 'Matthew 13:33', 'The kingdom of heaven is like yeast that a woman took and mixed into about sixty pounds of flour until it worked all through the dough.', NOW())
